      "evidence": "**Evidence supporting each level**\n\n- **Gone:** N/A.\n- **High Risk (candidate evidence):** The statute leaves content to the Secretary and sets no publication deadline, so \"what has to be collected\" is not enumerated line by line.\n- **Moderate Risk (candidate evidence):** NASS has itself argued that substitute sources exist for some collections (e.g., DOL's OEWS replacing the Farm Labor Survey).\n- **No Known Issue:** The census is **explicitly required** by the Census of Agriculture Act of 1997 (Pub. L. 105\u2011113), codified at **7 U.S.C. \u00a72204g**: the Secretary \"shall take a census of agriculture\" every fifth year, naming states and territories; specialty crops are statutorily required as part of it; response is mandatory. NASS and ERS are **OMB-designated Recognized Statistical Agencies and Units** (44 U.S.C. \u00a73563), and NASS operates under CIPSEA and 7 U.S.C. 2276 confidentiality. **No alternative collection substitutes for it** \u2014 it is the only source of uniform, comparable county-level U.S. agricultural data, and it is wired into federal program administration (e.g., FSA loan allocation formulas at 7 CFR 761.205; RMA yields and price elections; ARC/PLC parameters; socially-disadvantaged-farmer funding targets).\n\n**Assessment: No Known Issue.** Statutorily mandated, explicitly named, no substitute.\n\n---"
