      "evidence": "**Evidence by risk level**\n\n- **Gone:** N/A.\n- **High Risk:** There are partial substitutes for pieces of the concept \u2014 **QCEW** (universe counts, quarterly and lagged), **CPS** (household-based employment), **JOLTS** (which itself benchmarks to CES), and private products (ADP). The *CES itself* is not named in statute, and there is no statutory publication deadline for the monthly jobs report.\n- **Moderate Risk:** Authority is real but general: **29 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a71\u20132** (BLS shall \"acquire and diffuse\u2026 useful information on subjects connected with labor\"); the CES collection is cleared under **OMB control number 1220-0011**, whose supporting statement cites that statute. CES is **required for the implementation of federal statistical programs, not by name**: BEA uses CES employment and aggregate weekly earnings in the National Income and Product Accounts/personal income; BLS's LAUS program uses CES as its primary input for state/metro estimates; JOLTS uses CES employment as a monthly benchmark; the Federal Reserve, NBER business-cycle dating, and the Conference Board's Coincident Economic Index depend on it; CES is also the escalation/contracting basis historically (War/Navy Department escalation clauses). The Employment Situation is an OMB-designated **Principal Federal Economic Indicator**, and the administration's FY2026 policy explicitly protects PFEIs \u2014 a meaningful de facto protection.\n- **No Known Issue:** Arguable if one accepts PFEI status + explicit agency authorization + use in federal programs as satisfying the tier.\n\n**Most appropriate: Moderate Risk.** CES is not statutorily mandated by name and has no statutory release deadline, so its survival depends on executive-branch priority \u2014 which is exactly the axis on which it has been buffeted. But it is structurally embedded in federal measurement (BEA, LAUS, JOLTS, Fed) and no alternative collection can substitute for \"monthly establishment payroll employment by industry,\" which keeps the risk out of the High tier.\n\n---"
