      "evidence": "**Evidence by risk level**\n\n- **Gone:** No.\n- **High Risk:** Two independent triggers are met:\n  - **Leadership removed:** the President fired Commissioner **Erika McEntarfer on Aug 1, 2025**, hours after the July jobs report, without evidence of manipulation. Deputy Commissioner **William Wiatrowski** served as acting head for ~18 months until **Brett Matsumoto was confirmed (~Aug 2026)**; Bloomberg Law reported \"**a third of high-level roles**\u2026 vacant,\" and CAP put senior vacancies at **>30%**, concentrated in employment estimates.\n  - **\u226520% staff loss:** GovExec (Aug 13, 2026): BLS \"**cut its staffing by 20% between fiscal 2024 and 2026**\"; ASA's *Nation's Data at Risk*: \"BLS has lost an estimated **22%** in staffing since FY24\"; Bloomberg Law: total staffing down ~20% since Trump took office, citing former Commissioner Groshen.\n- **Moderate Risk:** Program-level budget: FY2026 request sought **\u2013$56.0M (\u20138%)** and **\u2013168 FTE**; the enacted FY2026 level was roughly **flat (+0.6% nominal, \u2248\u20132% real)**, so the funding trigger (\u226520% cut) was not met at BLS's topline.\n- **No Known Issue:** No.\n\n**Most appropriate: High Risk.** \"Leadership removed\" alone satisfies the High tier, and the ~20\u201322% workforce reduction independently approaches it. Note the mixed funding picture: the *proposed* BLS cut was not enacted for FY2026, but the FY2026 request assumed savings \"from staff attrition and **statistical agency reorganization**,\" and BLS's own capacity (field collection, senior statistician ranks) is materially reduced.\n\n---"
