      "evidence": "**Evidence supporting each level**\n\n**Gone**\n- No evidence. Pre\u2011current-year material remains publicly accessible.\n\n**High Risk**\n- No evidence that whole vintages of the release have been withdrawn.\n\n**Moderate Risk (evidence present)**\n- A **whole lender sector was permanently removed from the ongoing dataset**: the **nonfinancial business** sector was decommissioned with the May 2025 G.19 (published July 8, 2025). The Board states: *\"Our last data point is December 2019, and entries following this month will not be populated in the public repository.\"* Historical data through 2019 remains, but the sector exists no longer as a live series. (Board FEDS Note, July 8, 2025; G.19 Technical Q&A #23.)\n- Other pre\u2011current-year data elements have been dropped historically (e.g., the **48\u2011month new\u2011car loan rate** was retired in 2022 and replaced by the 72\u2011month rate; on\u2011book/off\u2011book lines replaced by \"total managed receivables\" in June 2020). These are element-level removals.\n- **Access pathway is being changed**: the Board is removing the DDP \"Build Your Package\" feature (week of Nov 9, 2026), removing preformatted packages, and **eventually retiring the DDP**, shifting users to FRED. Data remains (XML on release pages, FRED/ALFRED vintages), but the historical retrieval mechanism is being reconfigured. (Board DDP\u2013FRED notices, Dec 18, 2025 and July 16, 2026.)\n\n**No Known Issue (largely holds for the bulk of the data)**\n- Historical tables and PDFs remain on Board pages; **FRASER** holds scanned issues back to 1976; **ALFRED** provides vintages. The nonfinancial-business history is explicitly retained (\"continues to be available on the Data Download Program\").\n\n**Most appropriate: Moderate Risk.**\nRationale: the *bulk* of historical data remains accessible and no vintages have been pulled, but real **data elements have been removed from the dataset** (nonfinancial business sector; 48\u2011month car rate), and the primary historical-download pathway (DDP) is being retired. This maps to \"Some data elements that exist in the dataset prior to the current year or cycle are removed.\"\n\n---"
