      "evidence": "**Evidence supporting each level**\n\n- **Gone:** No. NASS still exists, publishes, and is staffed.\n- **High Risk:** Every trigger in the rubric is met or exceeded \u2014\n  - **\u226540% of staff lost:** ASA reports **839 FTEs (FY23) \u2192 389 (FY26) = 54%**; Amstat reports **~41% since FY24**; USDA's own notes show **754 \u2192 495**.\n  - **Budget:** FY25 $187.85M \u2192 FY26 request **$185.0M** (a ~1.5% cut, ~4% purchasing-power loss) \u2014 *below* the 20% budget trigger, but paired with a 40%+ headcount loss and further FY2027 reductions to **489 staff years**.\n  - **Leadership change:** NASS leadership and REE leadership were restructured in the **April 23, 2026** reorganization (\"leadership restructuring,\" \"strengthening leadership accountability\"); NASS's Administrator role has been in flux, and the discontinuation notice was signed by an **Acting Associate Administrator**.\n  - **Plus:** VERA/VSIP buyouts, a **Sept 21, 2026** relocation deadline, and a union survey showing **76% unwilling to relocate** \u2014 i.e., substantial *further* attrition is already in motion.\n- **Moderate Risk:** Would be the call if only the FY26 topline were considered (a ~1.5% reduction) \u2014 but the headcount data foreclose this.\n- **No Known Issue:** Not tenable.\n\n**Most appropriate level: High Risk**\n\nThis is the least ambiguous category in the assessment. A **54% reduction in FTEs in three fiscal years**, continued attrition via buyouts and forced relocation, and a restructured leadership layer satisfy the High Risk definition multiple times over. The USASpobs staffing tracker supplied by the user (**https://usajobs-tracker.abigailhaddad.com**) cannot corroborate the post-2025 picture: **it archives on December 31, 2025** and stops collecting data on that date, so it can speak to calendar 2024 vs. 2025 vacancy postings only. I therefore relied on the USDA budget documents, ASA, Amstat, and NSAC for the 2026 staffing facts. *(Note: that tracker measures job *listings*, not hires \u2014 even for 2024\u201325 it is directional only.)*\n\n---"
