      "evidence": "**Evidence supporting \"Gone\"** \u2014 None found. No indication that LIHEAP statistical files have been withdrawn.\n\n**Evidence supporting \"High Risk\"** \u2014 None found at file level. Older Reports to Congress (e.g., FY2013) and Notebooks (back to FY2007) remain online (acf.gov/sites/default/files/documents/ocs/fy13_liheap_rtc_final.pdf; liheappm.acf.gov/notebooks). Data Warehouse coverage still advertised as **FY2001\u2192present**.\n\n**Evidence supporting \"Moderate Risk\"** \u2014 Documented element-level contraction:\n- The Household Report reinstatement (91 FR 35691, 12 June 2026) **removes \"reporting requirements related to sex, race, and ethnicity\"** \u2014 elements OCS added as required items beginning with FY2023 (AT 2023-04, 9 June 2023) \u2014 and removes CARES Act/ARPA-specific data elements.\n- FY2026 Household Report instructions delete prior sections (including Sections VII and IX) and remove CARES/ARPA sections, following earlier item reductions.\n- Legacy preservation gap: the pre-migration Clearinghouse domain `liheapch.ncat.org` returns **no Wayback snapshots** (archive.org availability API check), so 1988\u20132010s Clearinghouse material is thinly archived.\n\n**Evidence supporting \"No Known Issue\"** \u2014 All prior-year products remain accessible: Grant Recipient Profiles FY2014\u2013FY2025, Reports to Congress FY2019\u2013FY2022 (current site) plus older ones on acf.gov, Home Energy Notebooks FY2007\u2013FY2022, Funding History tables, news archives 2020\u20132026, and the whole DW series.\n\n**Assessment: Moderate Risk.** No files have been taken down, so this is not High. But the rubric's Moderate condition \u2014 \"some data elements that exist in the dataset prior to the current year or cycle are removed\" \u2014 is met on the record: race/ethnicity/sex items introduced in FY2023 are being deleted from the instrument, ARPA/CARES breakdowns are gone, and report sections have been discontinued. A strict file-availability reading would score this \"No Known Issue,\" but the schema is demonstrably narrowing.\n\n---"
